{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXZavSHtRTf7RdZygZZf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's a plan built on what I know about Mila. Her birthday is Wednesday, 11 November.\n\n**Direction: a quiet evening with a little jazz, and no crowds.**\n- **Venue:** a small live jazz club, ideally one that seats 30–40 people. Reserve a table near the back or side so it feels private. Or skip going out and have dinner at home with a jazz record on.\n- **Her nut allergy:** she had a serious reaction at a restaurant recently. Tell the venue about it when you book and ask how the kitchen handles allergens. Desserts and sauces are where nuts usually hide. If you cook at home, you control all of it.\n- **Quiet on purpose:** after Lev's Lego party she said she wants a quiet evening next time. Keep it to just the two of you, with no surprise guests or group dinner.\n- **Vesna:** your mother-in-law arrives Monday 2 November for two weeks, so she'll be there on the 11th. She could watch Lev while you're out, or she could join for a short toast earlier in the day. It's worth asking Mila which she'd prefer.\n\n**Rough timeline**\n1. **This week:** pick the venue and book, or decide on dinner at home.\n2. **A few days before:** confirm the allergy arrangements and line up Vesna to watch Lev.\n3. **On the day:** have a small gift ready, plus flowers or a favorite dessert you've checked is nut-free.\n\nThree questions would help me narrow this down:\n1. Which city are you in? I can search for small jazz venues there.\n2. Do you want dinner out with jazz, or a home evening?\n3. What's your budget, and is there a gift idea yet?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16304,"cache_read_input_tokens":13147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16304},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"st